  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employers and business membership organizations play a key role in advocating for a conducive business environment that enables the creation and expansion of sustainable enterprises and decent jobs. They also have to provide services responding to enterprises&#x2019; needs that would contribute to improving their performance. In order to fulfil adequately this role, employers&#x2019; organizations need to be characterized by strong institutional capacity including good governance, financial sustainability and skilled human resources. 
In Liberia, as in other countries, private sector employers need a strong and trusted voice to lead advocacy for reforms of the business environment to foster entrepreneurship, enterprise development and the creation of decent jobs. To that effect, the ILO provided support in 2022-2023 to the most representative EBMO in Liberia for the development of a strategic plan that would provide guidance to its leadership in reviving the institution and enable it to carry out its core mandate, adhere to best practices and principles, represent enterprises &#x2018;interests and deliver the needed services to its members.
In 2024-2025, ILO strategy will continue to support strengthening the institutional capacity of the most representative EBMO. The ILO will focus on supporting the implementation of its strategic plan particularly regarding capacity building of staff, improved communication and services.</narrative>
  </description>
